---
import PageLayout from '@layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '@data/site';

const updated = '2026-07-01';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for AutoWarehouse by Intellica (a PiA Group company). Licensing terms, usage policies, and service level agreements."
>
  <!-- hero -->
  <section class="th grid-bg">
    <div class="shell th-inner">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1 class="th-h1">Terms of <span class="highlight">Service</span></h1>
      <p class="th-sub">
        AutoWarehouse is a product of Intellica — a PiA Group company. This document will be expanded with full
        licensing terms, usage policies, and service level agreements.
      </p>
      <div class="th-meta">
        <span class="pill">Document · TOS-001</span>
        <span class="th-updated">Last updated · {updated}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- prose -->
  <section class="shell tp">
    <article class="panel tp-panel reveal">
      <div class="tp-mark" aria-hidden="true">§</div>

      <div class="tp-block">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">01 · Acceptance of Terms</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          These Terms of Service (the "Terms") govern access to and use of the AutoWarehouse platform and the
          autowarehouse.ai website, provided by Intellica (a PiA Group company). By accessing this website, requesting a
          demo, or using the Platform, you agree to these Terms. Where a signed enterprise agreement exists between you
          and Intellica, that agreement controls and prevails over any conflicting provision here.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">02 · Definitions</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          "Platform" means the AutoWarehouse software — the application, AI/agent engine, LLM runtime, and related
          components deployed on the Customer's own infrastructure. "Customer" means the organization that licenses or
          uses the Platform. "Service" means the Platform together with any documentation, updates, and support
          Intellica makes available. "Content" means data, models, mappings, queries, and outputs that the Customer
          connects, creates, or processes through the Platform.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">03 · License Grant &amp; Restrictions</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          Subject to these Terms and any applicable enterprise agreement, Intellica grants the Customer a non-exclusive,
          non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to install and use the Platform for its internal business
          operations. The Customer may not reverse-engineer, resell, sublicense, or provide the Platform as a service to
          third parties, remove proprietary notices, or use the Platform outside the scope granted. All rights not
          expressly granted are reserved by Intellica.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">04 · Commercial Terms</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          AutoWarehouse is licensed under individual enterprise agreements; fees, deployment scope, and term are set in
          each Customer's agreement. Tier positioning is outlined on our <a href="/pricing"><u>pricing page</u></a>; a
          managed offering is forthcoming. For licensing, deployment, or commercial questions, reach our team.
        </p>
        <a class="tp-mail" href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>
          <span class="tp-mail-glyph" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          {CONTACT.email}
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">05 · Acceptable Use</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          The Customer agrees to use the Platform lawfully and only with data it is authorized to process. The Customer
          may not use the Platform to violate applicable law, infringe third-party rights, or attempt to disrupt, probe,
          or gain unauthorized access to Intellica systems or the website. Because the Platform is self-hosted, the
          Customer is responsible for its own infrastructure, access controls, and the data it connects.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">06 · Service Levels &amp; Support</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          The AutoWarehouse platform runs on the Customer's own infrastructure. Support scope, response targets, and any
          service-level commitments are defined in the applicable enterprise agreement or a separate SLA; no service
          levels are promised for the informational website itself. ETL execution is currently pre-alpha and provided
          without availability guarantees.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">07 · Intellectual Property</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          Intellica and its licensors own all right, title, and interest in the Platform, including its software,
          models, templates, and documentation. The Customer retains all ownership of its Content — its source data, the
          data warehouse it builds, agent state, and query results, all of which remain within the Customer's perimeter.
          The Customer grants Intellica no rights to that Content beyond what is necessary to provide support under an
          agreed engagement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">08 · Confidentiality</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          Each party may receive information the other treats as confidential. The receiving party will use such
          information only to perform under these Terms, protect it with reasonable care, and not disclose it except to
          personnel or advisors bound by comparable obligations. This does not apply to information that is public,
          independently developed, or lawfully obtained without a duty of confidentiality.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">09 · Warranties &amp; Disclaimers</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          This website and its contents are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, express
          or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. Any warranties
          for the Platform are limited to those expressly stated in the applicable enterprise agreement. Product
          descriptions on this site are informational and may change.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">10 · Limitation of Liability</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits or data, arising out of or relating to these Terms or
          use of the website. Any liability for the Platform is governed by, and capped as set out in, the applicable
          enterprise agreement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">11 · Indemnification</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          The Customer will defend and indemnify Intellica against third-party claims arising from the Customer's
          unlawful use of the Platform, its Content, or its breach of these Terms. Any reciprocal indemnities from
          Intellica — for example against claims that the Platform infringes third-party intellectual property — are set
          out in the applicable enterprise agreement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">12 · Term, Termination &amp; Suspension</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          These website Terms apply while you use the site. Platform license term, renewal, and termination are governed
          by the applicable enterprise agreement. Intellica may suspend or terminate access for material breach,
          unlawful use, or as required by law. Provisions that by their nature should survive — including intellectual
          property, confidentiality, and limitation of liability — survive termination.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">13 · Governing Law &amp; Jurisdiction</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Türkiye, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. The
          courts of Istanbul, Türkiye have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from these Terms, save where
          mandatory law provides otherwise.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tp-block divider-dashed">
        <div class="mono-label tp-k">14 · Changes to These Terms</div>
        <p class="tp-p">
          Intellica may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes take effect when the revised version is
          posted here, with the "Last updated" date above amended accordingly. Continued use of the website or Platform
          after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <aside class="tp-aside reveal">
      <span class="tp-aside-t">Looking for our data practices?</span>
      <a class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" href="/privacy">Read the Privacy Policy</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .th {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }
  .th-inner {
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .th-h1 {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    font: 900 clamp(38px, 6vw, 72px)/0.9 var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .th-sub {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    font: 400 clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 16px)/1.6 var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .th-meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }
  .th-updated {
    font: 700 10px var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  .tp {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }
  .tp-panel {
    position: relative;
    padding: clamp(26px, 4vw, 48px);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .tp-mark {
    position: absolute;
    top: -18px;
    right: 10px;
    font: 900 160px var(--font-display);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--line);
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .tp-block {
    position: relative;
  }
  .tp-block + .tp-block {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-top: 32px;
  }
  .tp-k {
    color: var(--orange);
  }
  .tp-p {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    max-width: 620px;
    font: 400 clamp(15px, 1.7vw, 17px)/1.7 var(--font-body);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .tp-mail {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 20px;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font: 800 13px var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--panel-2);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      border-color 0.2s,
      color 0.2s,
      transform 0.15s;
  }
  .tp-mail:hover {
    border-color: var(--orange);
    color: var(--orange);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }
  .tp-mail-glyph {
    font: 900 14px var(--font-display);
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .tp-aside {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: 12px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--yellow);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  .tp-aside-t {
    font: 600 13px var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
</style>
